apiVersion: kpt.dev/v1
kind: Kptfile
metadata:
  name: spectrum-exporter
  annotations:
    config.kubernetes.io/local-config: "true"
info:
  description: |
    The receive-only SDR spectrum exporter as a kpt package: a hardened
    Deployment that publishes per-band occupancy, peak power, and noise floor
    as Prometheus metrics, a ClusterIP Service, a ServiceMonitor so Prometheus
    scrapes it, and report-only alert rules. This puts sensed spectrum on the
    same observability plane as the operator's node health.

    Simulation-first and receive-only, like the mesh-gateway node: the shipped
    Deployment runs in -replay mode over a bundled sample sweep, so it is a real
    metrics source in a cluster with no radio and it renders and passes the
    manifest security gate (no hostPath, no privileged, no host namespaces). The
    real-SDR sensor path needs host USB access and runs outside this package; see
    the README.

    All resources are namespaced; set-namespace places them in the per-clone
    namespace.
pipeline:
  mutators:
    - image: ghcr.io/kptdev/krm-functions-catalog/set-namespace:v0.4.1
      configPath: package-context.yaml
    - image: ghcr.io/kptdev/krm-functions-catalog/set-labels:v0.2.0
      configMap:
        app.kubernetes.io/part-of: nephmesh
        app.kubernetes.io/managed-by: nephmesh-catalog
